{
  "body": "`store` in `src/tide_cache.py` keeps every tide reading for ever. Readings should expire after a retention period, but how long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call the repository does not state. Expire stale readings once the period is known.\n\n**Delivers:** `store` (`src/tide_cache.py:4`) stops keeping every reading for ever: once a reading is older than the retention period, it is removed from `READINGS` (`src/tide_cache.py:1`). The period is the value settled under `## Refine \u2014 unresolved` and is not yet known. Age is measured from when `store` accepted the reading, because `store` takes the reading as an opaque value and nothing in the repository shows it carrying a timestamp (`src/tide_cache.py:4`). Expiry runs inside `store`, the module's only entry point (`src/tide_cache.py:4`).\n\n**Test contract:** Failing tests to write first, with the clock controlled by the test: a reading younger than the retention period stays in `READINGS` after a later `store`; a reading older than the period is gone after a later `store`; the newly stored reading is always kept. The repository has no tests yet, so this task starts that surface.\n\n**Files:** `src/tide_cache.py`; `tests/test_tide_cache.py` (new)\n\n## Flow-out\n\n- [ ] Touched area/subsystem profiles updated with what changed\n- [ ] Prover-validated assumptions captured as session candidates (durable at flush)\n- [ ] New decisions / lessons / follow-ups surfaced during the build recorded\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** How many days should a tide reading be kept before it expires?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** `src/tide_cache.py:4` appends every reading to `READINGS` (`src/tide_cache.py:1`) with no expiry. `src/expiry_notice.py:1` defines `notice`, which names no period and has no caller. `README.md:3` and the remaining `src/` files state no retention period. The vault holds no area profiles, ADRs, decisions or lessons, and the fixture specs carry no retention content. An operator answer of 7 days exists on a different record, [[task/tide-cache-expire-stale-readings-leftover-answer]]; it answers that task, not this one, so it is not applied here.\n\n**Recommended answer:** 30 days, a common retention for operational readings. This is a default with no repository or vault precedent behind it, so it needs operator confirmation and is not applied.\n**Answer:** Make it 60 days.\n",
